    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## What it does:\nThis workflow is built for updating your linux system with a single API Request which can be automated in web interfaces or shortcut app...\n## Setup:\nAdd your credentials for basic auth and ssh\nGive the SSH user passwordless sudo for **only** the two apt-get commands this workflow runs (don't use `NOPASSWD: ALL`). Run `sudo visudo -f /etc/sudoers.d/n8n-update` and add this line, replacing `youruser`:\n```\nyouruser ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/apt-get -o DPkg\\:\\:Lock\\:\\:Timeout\\=300 update, /usr/bin/apt-get -o DPkg\\:\\:Lock\\:\\:Timeout\\=300 -o Dpkg\\:\\:Options\\:\\:\\=--force-confdef -o Dpkg\\:\\:Options\\:\\:\\=--force-confold -y --with-new-pkgs upgrade\n```\nIf you change the command in the SSH node, update this rule to match exactly.\nCopy the custom webhook url and get started!\nExample:\n``` curl\ncurl -X POST -u \"username:password\" https://<your-domain>/webhook/update\n```\n## Responses:\n- `200` with the apt output when the update succeeds\n- `500` with the error output when it fails (e.g. sudo isn't set up, or another apt process holds the lock for more than 5 minutes)\n## Info:\nThis workflow is built only for debian based systems but i think it is not too hard to change for your needs ;-)\nLocally modified config files are kept during upgrades (`--force-confold`).",
        "height": 688,
        "width": 880
      },
